              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HANLVY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good! I used Splenda instead of sugar and fat-free milk to make it a low-calorie drink. It was really good!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shannon"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Having made this smoothie so many times over the last couple years, I've found our favorite version: fill the blender about a quarter full of crushed ice, add a 1/2 c OJ (omit water), the OJ conentrate, 1/4 c sugar (or Splenda) a couple scoops of fat-free frozen yogurt, 1 tsp vanilla and 3 T malted milk powder (I'm convinced this is the ingredient needed to make this taste like a real Orange Julius!) I make these every summer (and whenever the craving arises), and these are always sooooo good!",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-10T21:18:36.493Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cookie2014"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This tastes just like an orange cream popsicle! It was very refreshing and creamy. A few changes were made. Instead of frozen orange juice concentrate, I used fresh squeezed orange juice, and then froze them as ice cubes. I did the same method for the milk. I left out the water all together. I drank half of the mixture, and then did something different. I added some frozen chopped Apricots to it and blended everything together. Very yummy!",
            "datePublished": "2014-06-16T14:55:26.890Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "marri_hampton"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love this! I am rating the original recipe here! However, I like to tweak things and play with recipes! I use all milk and no water and sometimes even replace some of the milk with whipping cream. My kids absolutely love this recipe!!! Such a treat in the morning!",
            "datePublished": "2017-09-10T13:22:22.053Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Frittsy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love this. - didn’t use any sugar and also added banana at the request of guests and it was yummy!",
            "datePublished": "2017-10-22T18:09:17.537Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "momto5"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This gets a five with the alterations I made. This is a great base recipe and have the basic ingredients I was looking for. I had a 12oz can of O.J. so I more or less doubled it. I used 1/2 &amp; 1/2 instead of milk, filled the empty O.J. can with ice water instead of two cups. Still only used 1/8 C of sugar. Used a whole tsp of vanilla, the real stuff not imitation and 24 Ice cubes. This was so very good. I think the 1/2 &amp; 1/2 and more vanilla really made it. The blender would not hold it all so I had to take about 1 1/2 cups out before adding the 24 ice cubes and then mix it back in after. Thanks for the recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2009-03-06T08:34:57.190Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RachelleBrazil"
            },
            "reviewBody": "instead of juice concentrate and water I simply used freshly squeezed orange juice.. way tastier and cost friendly when there's an orange tree in my yard!",
            "datePublished": "2017-05-01T19:33:53.267Z"
          },
          {
